                        "glosses": [
                            "The person who graduates high school with the second-highest GPA and thus gets to give the salutatory address during the graduation ceremony."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4393ba2a-341c-48c8-b8f1-6d91f0fb936f",
                                "sense_id": "66a65d17-2ce8-3c6b-9994-6d9ce0930d2d",
                                "text": "At first, it seemed a joyous occasion. There was an audible gasp in the room, then boisterous cheering and applause when the announcement was made: Ikeria Washington and Layla Temple had been named 2021 valedictorian and salutatorian for West Point High School. […] Within days, and breaking with longstanding tradition, West Point High School decided to name two valedictorians and two salutatorians — with two white students, Emma Berry and Dominic Borgioli, joining the Black students who had already been named."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cf93158-3eb3-4a82-8294-d4a726b507e7",
                                "sense_id": "66a65d17-2ce8-3c6b-9994-6d9ce0930d2d",
                                "text": "He was the salutatorian of his high school class (a sore subject, his sister said, since So thought he missed the top spot on a technicality), and entered Stanford intending to major in computer science."
                            }
                        ]
